  "baseline_rationale": "eso_scao_medium_12m_derived@2 with two reconstructor changes made after a comparison with a Fourier model and a scan of the Tikhonov factor in the production closed loop (2026-11-10 and 2026-11-11): reconstructor.waffle_filter_cutoff = 0.35, which removes the response's weakly sensed checkerboard family from every reconstructed increment, and reconstructor.alpha = 0.03 in place of 0.001.  On five noiseless realizations of 1000 frames (burn-in 100) the residual wavefront RMS is 183.16 +- 2.02 nm for version 2 and 172.10 +- 1.51 nm with the filter.  On twelve realizations of 600 frames the factor then lowers the residual variance by 431 +- 26 nm2 (172.31 to 171.06 nm), in every realization; factors of 0.03 and 0.05 are not distinguishable (41 +- 28 nm2) and 0.02 is 112 +- 10 nm2 worse.  With 1 e- of read noise at 1000 and 500 photons per sub-aperture and frame the residual variance falls by 348 +- 43 and 356 +- 78 nm2 on four realizations.  Every other value, including the atmosphere, the sensor and the 200-frame run length, is that of version 2, so the atmosphere and observing-condition identities are unchanged.",
